<title>FRANCE: France's high-speed trains go double-decker.</title>
<headline>France's high-speed trains go double-decker.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>France on Thursday introduced double-decker trains in its high-speed TGV service to cope with growing traffic on its busiest Paris-Lyon route.</p>
<p>The state railway company SNCF said the blue-and-grey trains carried 516 passengers, 40 percent more than a conventional TGV train, at the same speed of 270 kph (170 mph).</p>
</text>
